Switch to CSS Grid with minmax tracks and explicit breakpoints, removing fixed card widths.

```css
.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr; /* mobile-first */
  gap: 16px;
}

@media (min-width: 600px) {
  .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
}

@media (min-width: 900px) {
  .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
}

.card { width: auto; }
.container { box-sizing: border-box; max-width: 100%; padding: 16px; }
```

Explanation: Removing fixed widths lets cards flex to available track size. Grid gaps are included in track calculation, so at 768px the two tracks and one gap fit within the container without overflow. Using minmax(0,1fr) prevents content overflow from expanding tracks. Mobile-first media queries step from 1 to 2 to 3 columns at the specified breakpoints.

Debounce to limit frequency, render with minimal DOM mutations, and delegate events.

```javascript
const ul = document.getElementById('results');
const input = document.getElementById('search');

const debounce = (fn, ms) => {
  let t; return (...args) => { clearTimeout(t); t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), ms); };
};

input.addEventListener('input', debounce(e => {
  const q = e.target.value.toLowerCase();
  const next = data.filter(d => d.name.toLowerCase().includes(q));
  // Minimal update
  const frag = document.createDocumentFragment();
  for (const item of next) {
    const li = document.createElement('li');
    li.dataset.id = item.id;
    li.textContent = item.name;
    frag.appendChild(li);
  }
  // Replace children in one operation
  ul.replaceChildren(frag);
}, 150));

// Stable event listener
ul.addEventListener('click', e => {
  const li = e.target.closest('li');
  if (!li) return; // ignore background clicks
  console.log('open', li.dataset.id);
});
```

Justification: Debouncing prevents a re-render on every keystroke burst. Building in a fragment and replacing children once avoids repeated layout and preserves the focused input node (not replaced). Event delegation avoids reattaching listeners as the list changes. Scroll position of the page is unaffected because only list children are replaced, not the container or ancestors.

