Use Post/Redirect/Get (PRG) and Django's messages framework. On valid POST, redirect to the detail URL; on invalid POST, render the form with errors (no redirect).

```python
from django.contrib import messages
from django.shortcuts import redirect, render

@login_required
def task_create(request):
    if request.method == 'POST':
        form = TaskForm(request.POST)
        if form.is_valid():
            task = form.save(commit=False)
            task.owner = request.user
            task.save()
            messages.success(request, 'Task created')
            return redirect('task-detail', pk=task.pk)
        # invalid: fall through to render bound form with errors
    else:
        form = TaskForm()
    return render(request, 'tasks/form.html', {'form': form})
```

